    }
  }
  textarea.form-input {
    resize: vertical;
    min-height: 6.5rem;
  }
  /* A <select> keeps the same box but draws its focus indicator as an OUTLINE.
     Tailwind's focus:ring-* compiles to a box-shadow, and WebKit renders
     natively drawn form controls itself and drops box-shadow on them, so on
     Safari and iOS the ring above painted nothing on any of the seven selects
     on this page. The focus:outline-none that pairs with the ring then removed
     the only fallback, leaving those controls with NO visible focus indicator
     at all on every Apple device: a WCAG 2.4.7 failure.

     Measured in a real WebKit on 2026-09-06, not assumed: the select does
     enter :focus and :focus-visible and document.activeElement is correct, but
     its computed box-shadow stays `none` while focused, on the same class
     every passing text field carries.

     An outline paints on native controls in every engine and follows the
     border radius. Full Indigo at 2px, detached by a 2px offset, is exactly
     what the ring above draws (8.16:1 on Linen), so the indicator is
     unchanged to look at and now actually exists. Do not swap it back.

